# Programs & Volunteer Registration: What's Changing

**December 2024**  
**Target Launch:** March 1, 2025

---

## The Short Version

We're replacing Give Lively for event registration with a system built into our website. It will automatically sync with Salesforce, send confirmation emails, and make life easier for everyone.

---

## What We Heard

From our December meeting, these are the pain points we're solving:

- ❌ Creating events twice (website + Give Lively)
- ❌ Manually sending registration lists to hike leaders
- ❌ Weird formatting when exporting from Give Lively
- ❌ No automatic confirmation or reminder emails
- ❌ Volunteer signup buried and hard to find
- ❌ Manually adding volunteers to Salesforce

---

## What You'll Be Able To Do

### For Programs & Events

**Creating Events:**
- Add events directly in WordPress (one place, not two)
- Set all the details: date, time, location, fee, capacity
- Add accessibility info, what to bring, rules, family-friendly tags
- Events appear on the website automatically

**Registration:**
- Visitors register on our website with one click
- They get an automatic confirmation email immediately
- Their info goes straight to Salesforce (no manual entry)
- We'll know if they're a first-time visitor or returning

**For Hike Leaders (Phase 2):**
- Leaders can check their own registration lists online
- Download a list when they need it
- No more waiting for Paige to send it

### For Volunteers

- Dedicated volunteer page (easy to find)
- Simple signup form
- Automatic welcome email
- Info goes straight to Salesforce Volunteers
- Staff gets notified of new signups

---

## What Visitors Will See

### Event Listing Page
- All upcoming programs in one place
- Filter by: type (hike, workshop, etc.), date, location
- At a glance: title, date, location, free or fee

### Event Detail Page
- Full description
- Accessibility info (trail length, difficulty, conditions)
- What to bring / what to wear
- Rules (no dogs, etc.)
- Family-friendly badge
- Members-only indicator
- Big "Register" button

### Registration Form
- Name, email, phone
- How many people in your party
- Any notes or questions
- Submit → instant confirmation

